WEBVTT

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:04.600
A mysterious duelist challenged 
Sawatari to a duel.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.750
He used Xyz Summon and looked just like Yuya.

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:17.100
LDS Chairwoman Himika Akaba used Sawatari's 
incident as an excuse to invade You Show School.

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:18.700
Duel!

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:26.200
Implementing mass into Solid 
Vision has created Action Duels.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:34.380
In duels where the field, monsters and duelists 
become one, the people are caught in a frenzy of excitement!

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.400
Believe x Believe  Biri-Biri-Biri Buddies!

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:57.190
You!  The strongest card 
isn't about winning or losing

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:00.570
You!  At full speed  On the game

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:09.330
Swinging ma ma ma mind

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:13.880
The soul's pendulum  Ultimate confusion

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:16.080
Impulse  Got it got it

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:21.290
Tough battles  Real revolution

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:32.040
Everybody goin'  Break through the walls!

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:39.010
Infinite future  Get rid of indecision!

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:42.910
Make it Make it  Be courageous (Break it now)

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:46.330
Step ahead!  Take a step (Do it now)

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:56.610
The fun is only getting started!  
So everyone's a Believer!!

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:59.930
Believe x Believe  Biri-Biri-Biri Buddies!

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:09.980
Judgment of the Stars
Xyz User Hokuto Shijima

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:13.820
I won't let you have You Show School!

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:17.620
He has such spirit.

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:20.120
I wonder how long it will last.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:22.470
Hokuto!

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:26.070
Show him your power!

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:28.620
Understood, Chairwoman.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.130
I'll go first!

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:34.070
I summon Constellar Algiedi!

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:43.010
When it's successfully summoned, I can Special 
Summon one Level 4 Constellar monster from my hand!

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:46.270
I Special Summon Constellar Kaus!

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:50.050
Constellar Kaus's effect activates!

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:55.920
Twice per turn, I can change a 
Constellar monster's Level by 1.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:01.020
I use the effect once to increase 
Constellar Algiedi's Level by 1!

00:03:04.270 --> 00:03:09.570
Then I use the effect for a second 
time to increase Kaus's Level by 1.

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:18.920
I overlay Level 5 Constellar 
Kaus and Constellar Algiedi!

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:31.020
Light of the stars, shake 
the earth and descend!

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:35.420
Xyz Summon!

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:40.470
Rank 5 Constellar Pleiades!

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:45.270
This is Xyz.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:48.470
Rank?  It's not Level?

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:52.070
You don't even know about that?

00:03:52.070 --> 00:04:02.620
When you Xyz Summon, you use several monsters with the 
same Level to Special Summon an Xyz Monster from the Extra Deck.

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:06.660
Xyz Monsters have Ranks instead of Levels.

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:09.080
What are those lights swirling around it?

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:10.620
Overlay Units.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:15.370
Xyz Monsters use those lights 
to activate their effects.

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:19.950
I end my turn.

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:27.780
If Yuya Sakaki really attacked Sawatari, 
what will he do after seeing an Xyz Summon?

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:30.620
My turn!  I draw!

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:40.260
I set the Pendulum Scale with Scale 1 
Stargazer Magician and Scale 8 Timegazer Magician!

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:58.620
Now I can summon monsters between 
Level 2 and 7 simultaneously!

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:03.250
Swing, my soul's pendulum!

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:06.220
Draw an arc of light in the sky!

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:08.020
Pendulum Summon!

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:10.920
Come out, my monsters!

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:15.520
Performapal Sword Fish!

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:18.520
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.720
They're here!

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:23.870
It gives me shivers!

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:26.310
So this is Pendulum Summon.

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:30.310
You're not going to Xyz Summon?

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:33.920
I'm not the one who attacked Sawatari!

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:36.480
I've never Xyz Summoned before!

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:37.970
That's right.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:42.190
I have to believe what Yuya says.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:45.470
Whatever.  You're not worthy 
of being my opponent anyway.

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:48.570
I'll tell it to you straight.  You will lose!

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:52.900
I won't lose.  I'll win!

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:56.970
Performapal Sword Fish's effect activates!

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:05.370
Once per turn, your monster loses 600 
attack points until the end of the turn.

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:11.570
All right!  Now Odd-Eyes 
has greater attack points!

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:12.780
Let's battle!

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:16.620
Odd-Eyes attacks Pleiades!

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:21.580
This is within my expectations.

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:24.860
Constellar Pleiades's effect activates!

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:30.820
By using one Overlay Unit, one card 
on the field returns to the hand!

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:33.540
I choose Odd-Eyes!

00:06:35.350 --> 00:06:36.850
Odd-Eyes!

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:39.480
Yuya!

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:42.450
Ouch!

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:47.060
Everything you do is within my expectations.

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:48.690
Same for you.

00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:50.890
What will you do next?

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:55.130
Damn!  Sword Fish can't destroy Pleiades!

00:06:55.130 --> 00:06:56.680
What else can I do?

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:06.950
You're going for Action Cards.

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:13.550
There should be an Action Card where 
the shooting star fell on the temple.

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:23.250
Did you come here to look for this?

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:26.420
Impossible!  When did you get it?

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:29.680
I'm an expert on this field.

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:35.700
I know the exact timing of when and where a 
shooting star carrying an Action Card will fall.

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:47.710
See?  It's pointless.

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:51.320
Damn...

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:55.720
This is bad.  He's anticipating 
his every move.

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:59.450
He didn't lie when he said that 
he's an expert on this field.

00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:03.320
Yuya!  I'm sorry!

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:05.880
But get fired up!

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:08.380
Get your blood boiling!

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:15.820
Just in case you didn't know, you'll be 
disqualified if you don't play a card for over a minute.

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:20.480
If you don't want that to happen, you have 
to continue the duel or end your turn.

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:24.650
I set one card and end my turn!

00:08:25.050 --> 00:08:30.820
Sword Fish's effect ends, so Pleiades's 
attack points return to normal.

00:08:31.020 --> 00:08:34.060
His opponent is a bad match for him.

00:08:34.060 --> 00:08:40.500
Ever since I mastered Xyz Summoning, 
I've won 40 consecutive duels.

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:43.940
This will be my 41st victory in a row.

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:48.010
My turn!  Let's battle!

00:08:48.010 --> 00:08:51.750
Constellar Pleiades attacks Sword Fish!

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:56.680
Yuya!

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:01.680
You can't do anything against me.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:05.820
Sawatari is pathetic for 
being attacked by you.

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:09.280
You're wrong!  I didn't attack him!

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:10.520
It doesn't matter.

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:16.150
You're going to lose pathetically, and this 
school will be placed under LDS's control.

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:18.380
No!  I won't let that happen!

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:20.180
Then try to stop me.

00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:23.980
I set one card and end my turn!

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:32.020
As long as he has Constellar Pleiades, no matter how 
powerful the monster I summon, it will be returned to my hand.

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:36.820
But it only has one Overlay Unit left.

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:39.560
My turn!  I draw!

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:41.300
I'll do it again!

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:42.900
Pendulum Summon!

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:45.780
Come out, my monsters!

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:48.940
Performapal Turn Toad!

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:52.500
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:09:55.300 --> 00:10:00.020
Yuya, it's boring if you don't 
do more entertaining things!

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:02.450
I don't have time for entertainment!

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:08.260
I can't afford to lose this duel!

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:12.860
Odd-Eyes!

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:20.060
You turn your back on your opponent?

00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:23.060
What a courageous ace duelist.

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:29.780
He's so serious.

00:10:29.780 --> 00:10:36.050
His desire to protect You 
Show School has him tied up.

00:10:45.180 --> 00:10:46.420
Yuya...

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:49.600
There's an Action Card over there!

00:10:53.070 --> 00:10:56.370
I activate Constellar Pleiades's effect!

00:10:56.370 --> 00:11:02.300
By using one Overlay Unit, Odd-Eyes 
Pendulum Dragon returns to your hand!

00:11:05.860 --> 00:11:08.550
He did it at that exact time on purpose!

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:20.060
Yuya!

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:23.460
I activate the trap Performapal Revival!

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:30.670
When an effect makes my monster leave the field, I can 
Special Summon one Performapal monster from the graveyard!

00:11:38.620 --> 00:11:40.180
Well done!

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:43.140
That was dangerous!

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:45.180
You'll do anything to win?

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:46.740
That's not cool!

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:51.980
So you haven't given up yet.

00:11:53.260 --> 00:11:56.220
The Action Spell Cosmic Arrow!

00:11:57.230 --> 00:12:03.380
This card destroys a spell card that was 
added to your hand other than by drawing.

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:07.380
Too bad.  Just when you got it.

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:11.420
I end my turn!

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:16.620
But Pleiades now has zero Overlay Units.

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:21.020
My turn!  I draw!

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:25.500
I summon Constellar Sombre!

00:12:27.860 --> 00:12:30.930
Constellar Sombre's effect activates!

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:38.380
Once per turn, by banishing a Constellar monster in my 
graveyard, I can add a Constellar monster in my graveyard to my hand!

00:12:38.380 --> 00:12:41.660
I add Constellar Kaus to my hand!

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:47.820
And on the turn that this effect activates, 
I can summon one Constellar monster.

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:51.300
I summon Constellar Kaus!

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:56.140
Two monsters with the same Level.

00:12:56.140 --> 00:12:57.360
That means...

00:12:57.580 --> 00:12:59.020
I'm not done!

00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:01.780
I activate Constellar Kaus's effect!

00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:06.180
Twice per turn, I can raise 
a monster's Level by 1!

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:09.340
I select Sombre and Kaus.

00:13:09.340 --> 00:13:11.420
I raise their Levels by 1!

00:13:17.300 --> 00:13:19.750
Level 5!  Does that mean...

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:25.180
I overlay Level 5 Sombre and Kaus!

00:13:27.690 --> 00:13:29.790
Xyz Summon!

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:33.220
Rank 5 Constellar Pleiades!

00:13:35.260 --> 00:13:37.380
Another Pleiades.

00:13:38.620 --> 00:13:48.760
You probably thought that I used up all of Pleiades's Overlay 
Units so that it can't activate its effect anymore, but too bad.

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:51.260
That was also within my expectations.

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:54.210
And what you're doing is 
within my expectations.

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:56.460
I've met the requirements.

00:13:57.780 --> 00:14:03.760
I can Xyz Summon this card by 
using one Constellar Pleiades!

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:05.360
Another Xyz?

00:14:05.580 --> 00:14:08.420
The dazzling light rains down!

00:14:10.060 --> 00:14:11.940
Xyz Summon!

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:17.820
Appear, Rank 6 Constellar Ptolemy M7!

00:14:18.140 --> 00:14:23.300
A treasure as great as Pendulum 
Summon is wasted in this school.

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:29.110
The best plan for everyone is 
to put it under LDS's control.

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:34.140
Let's go, Turn Toad!

00:14:35.150 --> 00:14:36.220
I'll get it this time!

00:14:36.420 --> 00:14:38.180
You don't know when to give up.

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:41.540
I activate Constellar Pleiades's effect!

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:47.300
By using one Overlay Unit, Performapal 
Turn Toad returns to your hand!

00:14:54.810 --> 00:14:55.840
Let's battle!

00:14:55.840 --> 00:14:59.580
Pleiades, attack Sword Fish!

00:15:07.350 --> 00:15:08.540
Yuya!

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:09.540
Run away!

00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:10.520
There it is!

00:15:10.520 --> 00:15:12.620
Yuya!

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:18.780
If you want to win, then have 
courage and step forward.

00:15:20.380 --> 00:15:21.980
Step forward!

00:15:33.110 --> 00:15:34.460
Yuya!

00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:36.220
He did it!

00:15:36.220 --> 00:15:37.380
No way!

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:39.100
You're supposed to run away!

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:42.380
Doing what I'm supposed to 
won't get people excited!

00:15:42.380 --> 00:15:44.140
That's why you're Yuya!

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:45.460
I'm burning up!

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:47.020
You're cool!

00:15:47.020 --> 00:15:48.820
It gives me shivers!

00:15:48.820 --> 00:15:50.930
This strike will end you anyway!

00:15:50.930 --> 00:15:53.820
Ptolemy M7 attacks you directly!

00:15:54.980 --> 00:15:58.270
I activate the Action Spell Twinkle Comet!

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:07.730
Your monster loses 1000 attack points until the 
end of the turn, and you take 500 points of damage.

00:16:13.730 --> 00:16:15.460
How dare you!

00:16:15.460 --> 00:16:18.380
I won 40 in a row!

00:16:18.380 --> 00:16:22.530
I never lost any life points!

00:16:22.530 --> 00:16:25.330
He exceeded your expectations.

00:16:25.550 --> 00:16:29.680
I activate the Continuous 
Spell Constellar Tempest!

00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:36.640
I can activate this card when I have two or 
more Constellar Xyz Monsters on my field.

00:16:38.440 --> 00:16:40.410
Crumble!

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:44.840
This effect halves your life 
points at the end of the turn!

00:16:44.840 --> 00:16:47.190
I end my turn!

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:54.290
Ptolemy M7's attack points return to normal.

00:16:54.290 --> 00:16:58.660
I'll do whatever it takes 
to finish you next turn.

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:00.750
What do you think dueling is?

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:01.590
That's right!

00:17:01.590 --> 00:17:04.260
Be quiet!  Dueling is a battle!

00:17:04.260 --> 00:17:06.570
I'll do anything to win.

00:17:06.570 --> 00:17:08.010
You're wrong!

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:10.260
I...

00:17:11.770 --> 00:17:13.900
I don't want to hurt anyone!

00:17:15.370 --> 00:17:17.280
I don't want to hurt you.

00:17:21.590 --> 00:17:24.440
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:26.660
The fun is only getting started!

00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:30.700
My turn!  I draw!

00:17:31.420 --> 00:17:32.500
All right!

00:17:32.930 --> 00:17:36.880
I summon Performapal Trampolynx!

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:43.940
When it's successfully summoned, I can 
return one card on my field to my hand.

00:17:43.940 --> 00:17:48.040
I return Stargazer Magician to my hand.

00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:51.590
What about Pendulum Summon?

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:52.930
What happens to it?

00:17:52.930 --> 00:17:58.170
Since Stargazer left, 
this will take its place.

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:02.080
Performapal Turn Toad!

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:04.220
What?

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:06.040
Now observe!

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:14.130
I set the Pendulum Scale with Scale 3 
Performapal Turn Toad and Scale 8 Timegazer Magician!

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:28.350
Now I can summon monsters between 
Level 4 and 7 simultaneously!

00:18:28.350 --> 00:18:31.090
Swing, my soul's pendulum!

00:18:31.090 --> 00:18:33.820
Draw an arc of light in the sky!

00:18:33.820 --> 00:18:35.590
Pendulum Summon!

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:38.750
Come out, my monsters!

00:18:40.570 --> 00:18:44.790
First, I'll have Stargazer Magician reappear!

00:18:45.240 --> 00:18:48.940
Stargazer returns as a monster 
instead of a summoning gate.

00:18:48.940 --> 00:18:53.250
Today's main eventer arrives!

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:57.100
It's wild with two beautiful 
different-colored eyes!

00:18:57.100 --> 00:18:59.950
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:04.350
Constellar Pleiades's effect activates!

00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:09.020
By using one Overlay Unit, 
Odd-Eyes returns to your hand!

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:11.130
Its show is over.

00:19:11.130 --> 00:19:13.680
No, the main eventer is immortal!

00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:14.570
What?

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:17.640
Stargazer Magician's effect activates!

00:19:17.640 --> 00:19:25.140
Once per turn, when my Pendulum Monster 
leaves the field, it's Special Summoned again!

00:19:25.770 --> 00:19:30.120
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon reappears!

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:35.280
Hooray!  With Odd-Eyes's damage doubling 
effect, it can destroy Pleiades!

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:37.330
Didn't you listen to me?

00:19:37.330 --> 00:19:40.260
Xyz have Ranks instead of Levels.

00:19:40.260 --> 00:19:46.440
And Odd-Eyes doubles battle damage, 
not raise its attack points.

00:19:46.440 --> 00:19:48.170
So it can't win?

00:19:48.170 --> 00:19:52.040
Yuya said that the fun 
is only getting started.

00:19:52.570 --> 00:19:54.880
Time for the climax!

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:57.730
Turn Toad's Pendulum effect activates!

00:19:57.730 --> 00:20:03.250
A Pendulum Monster swaps its attack and 
defense points until the end of the turn!

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:06.660
I select Stargazer Magician!

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:16.530
I activate the spell card 
Magical Star Illusion!

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:21.940
When Stargazer Magician is on the 
field, until the end of this turn...

00:20:21.940 --> 00:20:30.730
...our monsters gain attack points equal to 
each player's total Level multiplied by 100 points!

00:20:30.730 --> 00:20:40.530
For Yuya's monsters, Odd-Eyes is Level 7, Stargazer 
is Level 5 and Trampolynx is Level 2 for a total of 14.

00:20:40.530 --> 00:20:43.720
They each gain 1400 attack points!

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:48.660
But his opponent's monsters 
gain attack points too.

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:50.880
Didn't you listen to me?

00:20:50.880 --> 00:20:54.480
Oh yeah!  Xyz don't have Levels.

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:56.640
So the opponent's attack points don't change!

00:20:56.640 --> 00:20:58.700
What?

00:20:58.700 --> 00:21:00.880
Here I go!

00:21:01.810 --> 00:21:07.810
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon 
attacks Constellar Ptolemy M7!

00:21:07.810 --> 00:21:10.380
Spiral Strike Burst!

00:21:14.150 --> 00:21:18.040
Stargazer Magician attacks Pleiades!

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:20.260
Horoscope Cutter!

00:21:24.350 --> 00:21:26.440
It's time for the finish!

00:21:26.440 --> 00:21:29.550
Trampolynx attacks you directly!

00:21:29.990 --> 00:21:33.550
My 41-match winning streak!

00:21:43.100 --> 00:21:44.520
That's one win for us!

00:21:44.750 --> 00:21:46.490
He did it!

00:21:46.490 --> 00:21:49.060
My blood is boiling!

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:56.660
Thank you!

00:21:59.330 --> 00:22:02.350
I don't want to hurt anyone!

00:22:03.330 --> 00:22:05.420
I don't want to hurt you.

00:22:06.750 --> 00:22:07.990
Yuya...

00:22:13.430 --> 00:22:18.910
Catch the dream dancing in my heart
Release my falling tears

00:22:19.130 --> 00:22:28.390
I'll step out on to my first field
To meet my miracle  Fabulous One Step

00:22:35.280 --> 00:22:40.400
I realized that strength can't be given

00:22:40.660 --> 00:22:45.640
It's something I have to grab myself

00:22:45.930 --> 00:22:51.080
In that case, I have to keep moving
I can't stay still

00:22:51.330 --> 00:22:56.340
Even if walls and headwinds block my way

00:22:56.540 --> 00:23:01.940
I'll draw my trump card called 
"courage" to take a step forward

00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:06.360
I believe in my story of victory

00:23:06.650 --> 00:23:12.330
Everyone during battle is My Way
Duelists are being tested

00:23:12.330 --> 00:23:17.740
When times are tough, that's when you 
Smile, Jump, Fight & Step Up!

00:23:17.740 --> 00:23:23.040
Your smile is your Energy
Kick away your feelings of running away

00:23:23.040 --> 00:23:32.380
Jump into the new field
Shiny One Step that leads to the future

00:23:33.410 --> 00:23:40.630
One step... Just one step is fine
That's your Big Chance!!

00:23:45.680 --> 00:23:50.170
The secret stone enveloped in lightning!  
The glimmering green that brings luck!

00:23:50.170 --> 00:23:54.050
The swirling light combines 
into a new brilliance!

00:23:54.220 --> 00:23:55.820
Fusion Summon!

00:23:55.820 --> 00:23:59.990
Appear, the seeker of 
victory!  Gem-Knight Topaz!

00:23:59.990 --> 00:24:03.790
She used Fusion Summon on her first turn?

00:24:03.990 --> 00:24:06.440
Your eyes are clouded.

00:24:06.440 --> 00:24:11.950
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V:
Knight of the Secret Stone!  Fusion User Masumi Koutsu

00:24:11.950 --> 00:24:14.220
The fun is only getting started!
